# starters/projektschau-kern/.cut -- which paths of The New Vienna make up site/.
# One path per line, relative to the full site's root. A directory copies
# recursively. Regenerate from the root of this repository with:
#   scripts/cut-starter.sh <path-to-the-full-site> projektschau-kern
#
# The Projektschau starter: Don Ludwig's Projektschau for KERN board drawn
# over a folder of project pages, filled with the City of Vienna's municipal
# programme, 1919-1934. Three projects in each of the five areas, covering
# all four kinds (Building, Service, Programme, Event) with the timeline
# still running from 1917 to 1934, the three projects the home highlights,
# the partners those projects name, and the German mirror of every kept page.

# moss's own scaffold: the gitignore and the empty redirects map.
.moss/.gitignore
.moss/redirects.json

# site config: the partners term and the kind/years/figure fields the board
# reads (their `in` lists name the five area folders and de/, all kept)
.moss/config.toml

# Projektschau, carried as a site plugin: donludwig's unmodified renderer
# (projektschau.js, projektschau.css, LICENSE.txt) and the moss port
# (main.js, engine-shim.js, manifest.json). The port's development test,
# test.js, is left out: it needs a moss build list and no user runs it.
.moss/plugins/projektschau/LICENSE.txt
.moss/plugins/projektschau/engine-shim.js
.moss/plugins/projektschau/main.js
.moss/plugins/projektschau/manifest.json
.moss/plugins/projektschau/projektschau.css
.moss/plugins/projektschau/projektschau.js

# theme: KERN tokens and the board's cut of the KERN kit, the dark-mode
# mirror script, and KERN's Fira Sans with the kit's licence
.moss/theme

# home (the board, its intro band and the three highlights), footer, About
# the sources, and the two root pictures (the home band's facade photograph
# and About's cover of Das Neue Wien)
index.md
footer.md
About the sources.md
Karl-Marx-Hof facade.jpg
Das Neue Wien cover.jpg

# Housing: the highlighted programme, its tax (a Programme with a money
